      "query": {
        "prompt": "Question 40/40\n\nFor active office products still in the catalog, bucket list price into four bands: under $15, $15 up to $30, $30 up to $60, and $60 or more. Within each band, take the average star rating among verified-purchase reviews only. What is the gap between the best and worst of those four band-level averages? Round to 2 decimal places.\n\nYou have access to a SQLite database that contains three separate product datasets covering different categories: office products, electronics, and musical instruments. Each dataset has its own set of tables. You will need to explore the schema to determine which tables belong to which product category.\n\nYou may run up to 15 exploratory SQL queries to examine the schema and data before submitting your final answer. Note: query results are capped at 50 rows — if a query would return more, only the first 50 rows are shown. Use aggregates, LIMIT, or filters when you need to inspect larger tables.\n\nActions:\n  QUERY  — run a SQL statement (SELECT, .tables, PRAGMA, etc.)\n  ANSWER — submit your final answer as the exact value (e.g. '50000', '3.14', 'Acme Corp'). Do NOT describe how to get the answer; provide the actual result.\n\nQueries used so far this question: 0/15",
        "instance_id": "116",
        "instance_index": 39,
        "metadata": {
          "question_id": 116,
          "question_num": 40,
          "difficulty": "hard",
          "queries_used": 0,
          "query_budget": 15,
          "db_path": "/tmp/tmpez8b8v3x.db"
        },
        "response_schema": "DatabaseAction",
        "feedback": null
      },
      "response": {
        "action": {
          "action": "QUERY",
          "content": "WITH band_ratings AS (SELECT CASE WHEN i.prc < 15 THEN 1 WHEN i.prc < 30 THEN 2 WHEN i.prc < 60 THEN 3 ELSE 4 END AS band, AVG(f.rtg) AS average_rating FROM items_g1 i JOIN fdbk_g1 f ON f.ref_id = i.ref_id WHERE i.status = 'active' AND i.prc IS NOT NULL AND f.vrf = 1 GROUP BY band) SELECT ROUND(MAX(average_rating) - MIN(average_rating), 2) AS gap FROM band_ratings;"
        },
        "action_type": "structured",
